Every applicant for a license to sell wine shall file with the clerk of the board of commissioners an application under oath in such form as may be provided by such commissioners at least ten days prior to the next regularly scheduled or called meeting of such commission disclosing the following:
(1) Type of license desired (on-premises or off-premises consumption);
(2) Name and address of the applicant and previous address if present address is less than one year duration;
(3) Length of time a resident of the state and of the county;
(4) The applicant's social security number;
(5) Type, number, location, and description of any other licenses for the sale of wine, malt beverages or spirituous liquors held by the applicant at the time of application;
(6) Age, sex, height, and weight of applicant;
(7) Names and addresses of real owner or owners of business and location for which a license is desired and, if different from or additional to applicant, all information as to such owner or owners as is required of the applicant;
(8) Location of business for which a license is desired;
(9) A complete set of fingerprints if the applicant through such facilities as may be provided for by the board of commissioners to be forwarded to the Georgia Bureau of Investigation pursuant to O.C.G.A. § 3-3-2;
(10) Three credit references and three personal references for applicant; and
(11) In the case of a corporation, a nonprofit corporation or a private club, the following requirements are applicable:
a. Corporation:
1. Copy of Charter;
2. List of officers and directors of corporation;
3. List of any stockholders owning more than one percent of the outstanding common or preferred stock of the corporation.
4. Affidavit of chief executive officer of the corporation under oath that the corporation has authorized properly the individual making the application for such application for such corporation who is either an officer of or is employed by and is responsible for the active management of the corporation's activities regarding the sale of wine at the time of the application.
5. Separate applications shall be received from both the individual designated in subsection (11)a.4 of this section, and from the chief executive officer of such corporation.
b. Nonprofit corporation or private club:
1. Copy of charter;
2. List of officers and directors of corporation;
3. Copy of Internal Revenue Service tax exemption letter;
4. List of officers and directors of corporation;
5. Affidavit of chief executive officer of the corporation under oath, stating the corporation is operated as a private club admitting only members and their invited guests; and that the corporation has authorized properly the individual applicant who is employed by and is responsible for active management of the corporation's activities regarding the sale of wine at the time of the time of application.
6. Separate applications shall be received from both the individual designated in subsection (11)a.5 of this section, and from the chief executive officer of such corporation.
As a prerequisite to the issuance of any such permit or license, the applicant shall furnish a complete set of fingerprints to be forwarded to the Georgia Bureau of Investigation, which shall search the files of the Georgia Crime Information Center for any instance of criminal activity during the two years immediately preceding the date of the application. The Georgia Bureau of Investigation shall also submit the fingerprints to the Federal Bureau of Investigation under the rules established by the United States Department of Justice for processing and identification of records. The federal record, if any, shall be obtained and returned to the governing authority submitting the fingerprints.
(Ord. No. 88-005, § 8, 5-3-1998)
State law reference— Powers of local governing authorities, O.C.G.A. § 3-3-2.

